Feature capture: a model calls web_fetch with no toggle, and the sources render
==============================================================================

PR      #1730, issue #1718 (refs #1621)
Run     https://github.com/sakibsadmanshajib/hive/actions/runs/33696844690
        workflow "chat visual proof", scenario=webtools, on refs/pull/1730/merge
Stack   Booted in CI on a hosted runner from the pull request's own merge ref,
        with this run's own Supabase, its own registered OAuth client, its own
        throwaway Postgres carrying the full migration chain, and the real
        "Continue with Hive" sign-in journey. Not the deployed box.
Images  Posted on the pull request from the permanent visual-proof-assets
        release: https://github.com/sakibsadmanshajib/hive/pull/1730#issuecomment-5518213458

WHY THIS CAPTURE EXISTS ALONGSIDE THE GENERIC ONE

The chat visual proof that runs on every chat pull request asks what colour a
banana is. That proves the signed-in surface is healthy, and it cannot prove
anything about this branch: a banana triggers no search. This run asks a
question the model cannot answer from memory instead.

WHAT WAS ASSERTED BEFORE THE CAPTURE, IN THE JOB ITSELF

  GET /v1/tools, unauthenticated, the exact form the chat shim sends: 200,
  serving web_search and web_fetch. Measured at 401 on run 33694706249, before
  the selector exemption in commit ad05537c7; that run is the reason this
  assertion exists.

  The model listing edge-api serves reports hive_capabilities.tools = true for
  hive-free and false for deepseek-v4-flash. That field is the only fact
  deploy/docker/owui-patches/hive_web_tools.py consults before it attaches a
  tools array, so it is the gate itself rather than a proxy for it.

THE NEGATIVE CONTROL IS CONSTRUCTED, AND SAYS SO

Every chat capable alias in the shipped catalog is tool capable, and the three
that are not (hive-embedding-default, hive-stt, hive-tts) have no chat route at
all, so a turn on one would fail at routing and prove nothing about
advertisement. The job therefore cleared tools_supported on deepseek-v4-flash's
routes IN THIS RUN'S OWN THROWAWAY DATABASE and asserted the clear took. What it
exercises is the real gate over a real catalog row.

WHAT THE GATEWAY LOGGED

Nothing, and that is the current state rather than a failure: edge-api logs a
webtools line only when a call fails, and the chat shim logs only when it
advertises nothing, so a served tool call is silent on both. SearXNG logged no
query either, correctly: the model chose web_fetch, not web_search. The visible
evidence of the call is Open WebUI's own "View Result from web_fetch" chip in
the third and fourth screenshots.

